# Non-negotiables

- Never invent URLs, participant names, metrics, testimonials, logos, or credentials.
  If a real value is missing, insert `TODO({field})` and stop to ask.
- Placeholder participants are marked `status: "pending"` in the data layer and render
  as visibly-pending cards. Never fabricate a finished profile.
- No merging PRs. No direct pushes to `projects/*` or `cohorts/*`.
- PR title must be exactly: [Project 3] Submission — ryanroper79-alt
- Do not add merge preconditions absent from the brief (e.g. user signup counts).

# Stack conventions

- Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Tailwind. Server Components by default;
  "use client" only where interaction demands it.
- Participant data lives ONLY in data/participants.ts, typed. No fetching at runtime.
- All profile routes statically generated via generateStaticParams.
- `npm run build` and `tsc --noEmit` must pass before any commit.
- Every participant surface must render at 0, 1, and 30 participants.

# CEAL Green voice (Brand Guidelines v0.2)

- Source: https://peteranthonygales.craft.me/s3ywHY5a1ppmyU — see `data/brand-guidelines.ts`
- Present tense. Declarative. Caribbean always visible. Warm, not transactional.
- Avoid: "sustainable future", "green transition", "transition", blame/diagnostic framing, defiance language, future "will" where "do" is accurate.
- Visual palette from logo until Guidelines §5 ships; do not invent designer hex values.
